      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-37376",
      ":question/problem": "A rehabilitation center initially has $20$ children. The number of children in the center $R(t)$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t \\ge 0$ is the time in months. If the maximum capacity of the center is $85$ children, which differential equation could be used to model the population of the rehabilitation center? Assume that $k > 0$ is a constant of proportionality."
