      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-335135",
      ":question/problem": "A wildlife manager noted that the growth of the number of deer in a protected forest is directly proportional to the difference between the forest\u2019s maximum deer population and the current population. Let $N(t)$ be the deer population, measured in number of deer, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in years. If the maximum deer population that the forest can support is $150$ deer, which differential equation could be used to model the forest\u2019s deer population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality."
